the las vegas veterans day parade  returns tomorrow was canceled last year  because of the pandemic this was  actually video then from two years ago  tomorrow's parade starts at 10 a.m it's  going to be in downtown las vegas at  fourth and gas we should have some great  weather for it  it will feature a four plane flyover and  120 different groups including of course  vets bands and rot rotc units so  tomorrow is veterans day when our nation  comes together to honor the incredible  sacrifices made by the men and women in  our military those who have received a  purple heart were wounded while serving  our country kate houston live in studio  after attending a very special ceremony  for our local purple heart veterans  yes four purple heart veterans were  honored today and since their service  these vets have dedicated their time to  supporting the more than 200 thousand  veterans all across nevada they're  advocating to end homelessness and  provide more mental health resources  daniel peterson served nearly 25 years  as a helicopter pilot he did two tours  in vietnam granada and desert storm  where his helicopter was shot down twice  peterson himself has been shot seven  times he now runs the purple heart  chapter in henderson advocating for 130  local veterans peterson says a key issue  right now is suicide all of us  veterans who have served have ptsd  you know i go to group counseling  that's what keeps me going so  we fear for what's going to happen with  them you know they've got it they've got  to get out there and get help u.s  senator catherine cortez masto  congresswoman susie lee and henderson  mayor deborah march attended the  ceremony at bellavita to help shine a  light on the issues veterans are facing  today during that time peterson was  recognized by 15 major organizations  they say he is one of the most decorated  veterans in the country and a national  hero  all of the money raised today will go to  veterans organizations bellavita  restaurant is 